1 NOTE
2 CONT Marriage Certificate; SL End. Rec. Film 184,067; Archive Stamp; Records of
2 CONT Edward James Tree, by his grandson, Albert W. Tree, 5243 W. 3990 S. Salt Lake
2 CONT City, Utah.
2 CONT FGR as child lists death date as 12 Oct 1923.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1851 Census Bearsted, Maidstone Film 0193517:
2 CONT 120 Rose Acre
2 CONT Edward Tree was 66 a widower, an Ag. Laborer, and born in Marden, Kent.
2 CONT John R. Tree was married, age 28, a shoemaker (journeyman), born in Bearsted, Kent.
2 CONT Mary A. Tree was son's wife, age 27, born Hauts, Mill Brook.
2 CONT Edward J. Tree was son, unmarried, age 19, Ag. Laborer and born in Bearsted, Kent.
2 CONT In 1860 on Frederick Tree's birth certificate, Edward James Tree was listed as a farm labourer.  The birth certificate is in the district Maidstone, sub-district Loose, County, Kent.
2 CONT Edward James is living with his father, Edward Tree in the 1861 Census in Bearsted, Kent, England.  He and his 75 year old father are listed as "ag laborers".
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1881 British Census Edward J. Tree is widowed, 50 years old, and listed as "ag laborer."
2 CONT 1881 British Census says that their address was:  35 Tovil Hill, East Farleigh, Kent, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Fern G. Hess copied down the following from a placard on Her Majesty's Theatre while on a visit to London:  "Her Majesty's Theatre, London, England.  Founded by Herbert Tree in 1897, actor and directed by him until his death in 19
2 CONC 17."  I don't know of any relation to this man, but perhaps he is distantly related to Edward James.  He would be contemporary with him at least.
2 CONT
2 CONT Came to America in 1884 with 2 daughters to join his son, Frederick.  Left 3 daughters behind.
1 CHAN
2 DATE 15 NOV 2014
3 TIME 06:32:56
