1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The Doyle family emigrated from Ireland, 1849. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The ship 'Mailand' Passenger List records: Doyle James, Labourer age 32, from Arklon County, Wicklow, Ireland. Mary, Housekeeper age 23, -- Catherine, Daughter age 1 1/2 years. Eliza, Born at sea.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth herself claimed 'Maitland' as her second name!
2 CONT
2 CONT The 'New South Wales Roman Cathlic Baptisms Register, for 1850' records the baptism of Eliza Doyle: 11 February, 1850 at St. Francis Church Melbourne. The date given: 24 November 1849, and her mother's maiden name as 'Murtha' (Gae
2 CONC lic for Murphy).
2 CONT
2 CONT The Doyle family settled in Benalla. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth married William Arch 3/6/1880, at Christ Church, Castlemaine. He was 20 and resided at Joyces Creek, Maldon,  He declared his age as 21. Elizabeth declared she was a 28 year old servant born in Benalla when in fact she w
2 CONC as 31 years old, born at sea! Elizabeth died of heart attack aged 61 at Portuguese Flat, Creswick. The verdict of a Coronial Inquiry 20/9/1913 recorded: death due to heart failure.     
