1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Teague Harrigan came to England from Cork, Ireland. He was tried on the charge of stealing clothing to the value of 20 shillings and was sentenced to transportation for 7 years. He was embarked on the ship "Salaman
2 CONC der" which sailed from Plymouth with 160 male convicts 27 Mar 1791 arriving Port Jackson 21 Aug 1791. The "Salamander" was sent to Norfolk Island arriving there 4 Sep 1791.
