3 STAE NSW
3 CTRY Australia
1 DEAT
2 DATE 17 DEC 1859
2 PLAC Fairy Meadow, New South Wales, Australia
2 ADDR
1 OCCU (a) Convict. Sentenced to be hung. Transported to Australia for life, aged 11 years ! (b) Street Sweeper - Wollongong.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Mary WADE''' was born on October 5, 1777 in Southwark, UK and was baptized on December 21, 1777 in St Olave Southwark, Camberwell, Greater London, UK. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-129201953 George WADE] and [h
2 CONC ttps://www.geni.com/profile-129201958 Mary ENGLISH]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT At age 10 on 14/1/1789 at Old Bailey, Mary (with [https://www.geni.com/people/Jane-Whitting-Kidner-Convict-Lady-Juliana-1790/6000000024050872835 Jane WHITING]) was convicted of Violent Theft and highway robbery and was sentenced t
2 CONC o death.  
2 CONT On 22/4/1789 her sentenced was commuted to transportation for life.  She left England in June 1789 and arrived in Sydney Cove on 3/6/1790 on "Lady Juliana".
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary was sent to Norfolk Island arriving on 7/8/1790
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary had a relationship with [https://www.geni.com/profile-129201702 Edward Teague HARRIGAN] c1791. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT * 1792 [https://www.geni.com/profile-129201992 Edward ]; died young
2 CONT * 1793 [https://www.geni.com/profile-34702803494 Sarah Mary];
2 CONT * 1795 [https://www.geni.com/profile-40086516 William ];
2 CONT * 1803 [https://www.geni.com/profile-34721190898 Edward ]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1806 her husband Edward left on a sealing expedition on "Fox" and did not return.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary married [https://www.geni.com/profile-40086882 Jonathon BROKER / BROOKER] on February 10, 1817 in Liverpool, New South Wales, Australia. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT * 1809 [https://www.geni.com/profile-34635918396 John ];
2 CONT * 1810 [https://www.geni.com/profile-129202277 Elizabeth ];
2 CONT * 1812 [https://www.geni.com/profile-129202360 Mary ];
2 CONT * 1814 [https://www.geni.com/profile-111377555 James Albert ];
2 CONT NOTE: There is some researchers who believe she had 21 children - sources are required in order to add the additional children to her profile.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary received her certificate of freedom on 1/9/1812
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1820 Mary's husband Jonathan petitioned the government for a land grant (stating he has a wife and 7 children, 5 of which he supports)
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1828 Mary, her husband Jonathan and 4 children (Edward, John, Mary, James) appear in the Australian Muster (Census)
2 CONT
2 CONT Her husband Jonathan died 14/3/1833
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary died on December 17, 1859 in Fairy Meadow, New South Wales, Australia and was buried in December 1859 in Pioneer Rest Park aka St Paul's Church of England Cemetery, Wollongong, New South Wales, Australia. 
2 CONT ----
