1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mary Wade’s second son, William, was born on Norfolk Island in 1796. As he is listed in the Victual Book of that year as – “Wade ‑ convict’s child,” there is no clear identity of his father. Mary, on her return fro
2 CONC m Norfolk, shared consecutive relationships in New South Wales with Teague Harrigan and Jonathan Brooker, both of whom were convicts on Norfolk Island at the time of William’s birth. However, her long- standing relationship was wi
2 CONC th the latter, who became the father figure in William’s life. 5th April 1821 William became a landholder at Airds, on receipt of a Macquarie grant of 60 acres. It would appear that he had learnt the carpentry trade from his fathe
2 CONC r and that he worked as a carpenter and joiner in the Campbelltown area.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT 1828 Census aged 33yrs
