1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Amos CRISP  was born c1790 Brandon, Norfolk, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Amos married Elizabeth Ann BROWN on 9/9/1810 England, UK and they had the following children
2 CONT * Amos 1812
2 CONT * Elizabeth 1812
2 CONT
2 CONT Amos was convicted of theft and sentenced to transportation for life. He arrived in Sydney Cove on 30/1/1816 on "Ocean".  His wife and children followed him to Australia arriving on "Lord Melville" in 1817
2 CONT
2 CONT After arriving in Australia, Amos and Elizabeth had the following children
2 CONT * Frances 1818
2 CONT * John 1819
2 CONT * Charles Lake 1821
2 CONT * Edward Luke 1823
2 CONT
2 CONT Amos married Mary BULL on 9/2/1830 at Liverpool, NSW
2 CONT
2 CONT Amos married Mary RAY in 1831 
2 CONT
2 CONT Amos married Louisa MARSTON
2 CONT
2 CONT Amos died 31/1/1881 at Windelama, NSW
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT LINKS
2 CONT * https://convictrecords.com.au/convicts/crisp/amos/109079
2 CONT * https://australianroyalty.net.au/individual.php?pid=I72784&ged=purnellmccord.ged
2 CONT * http://www.members.optusnet.com.au/~aashmore/ElizbWms.htm
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Crisp-107
2 CONT * http://www.monaropioneers.com/crispa.htm
2 CONT * http://www.lunatribe.com/Genealogy/13722.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-1-135228501-1-90/amos-crisp-born-crisp-junior-in-myheritage-family-trees?indId=externalindividual-c5f0bca4ddbaa188cae3c76e1abc2264&mrid=eecc64c70420ef3d29f602678986f820 MyHe
2 CONC ritage Family Trees] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 23 2018, 8:23:23 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-1-175296531-5-1522/amos-crisp-in-myheritage-family-trees?indId=externalindividual-76da0e0b0fbc3ad91409d742e8af6c65&mrid=e4503a4f863678dd5bc8b2c196ce48e0 MyHeritage Family Tr
2 CONC ees] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 25 2017, 22:14:04 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT Sentenced to death, commuted to "Life in the colonies". aliases: Amos Vince
2 CONT
2 CONT Anonymous on 30th March, 2012 wrote:
2 CONT
2 CONT Under Amos Ames - Old bailey on line: Sentenced to death for stealing 1 watch, value of 12pound 1s. the property of Robert Tulloch.
2 CONT
2 CONT Col.Sec: 5/2/1816 - On list of convicts forwarded to Liverpool for distribution. 17/12/1819 - Received payment at Sydney for meat and grall deliverer=d to the Commissariat Stores. 24/12/1820-24/1/1821 - Store receipts for fresh me
2 CONC at. 1830 TOL.
2 CONT
2 CONT Amos was married to Elizabeth Ann Brown (1785-1827) on the 9/9/1810. After Amos had been transported Elizabeth travelled to NSW on the Lord Melville 1817 with her son, Amos, and a daughter.  Amos (convict) became involved in activ
2 CONC ities of dubious legality and was eventually forced to flee the country.  His famils is well documented in the Monaro Pioneers website.  He died on the 31/1/1881 at Windellama, Southern Tablelands.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah on 20th September, 2018 wrote:
2 CONT
2 CONT Amos CRISP (convict) was the son of Amos CRISP, whose sister Susan married Philip VINCE.
2 CONT
2 CONT Amos VINCE (a blacksmith in Wereham, Norfolk) was the son of Philip and Susan VINCE, and thus the cousin of the convict Amos CRISP.
