1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sydney Free Press (NSW), Saturday 31 July 1841, page 3
2 CONT
2 CONT " Staff of Life." — We have been requested to state, in reply to a letter with the above signature, which appeared a few day's since in the Monitor, that the proprietor of the Brisbane Steam Flour Mills Bakery, is Mr. H. S. Hayes,
2 CONC  who also carries on the business of a miller both at the Brisbane Mills and at the South Head Road Windmills. Mr. H..has, we believe, but recently arrived in the colony, and the undertaking of the bakery in which he has at once e
2 CONC mbarked, affords an abundant -proof of his enterprising nature. His undertaking is certainly a very spirited one, and is calculated to be productive of highly important results to the public, for which reason we most sincerely joi
2 CONC n in wishing that it prove successful.
2 CONT
2 CONT New South Wales death registration index record for Henry S Hayes, father Henry, mother Mary, Forbes registration district, No. 6878 of 1881 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sydney Morning Herald (NSW), Saturday 15 January 1881, page 1
2 CONT
2 CONT HAYES.-January 8, at his daughter's residence, Bogabagill, Forbes, Mr. H. S. Hayes, late of this city, aged 80 years.
