1 NOTE {geni:about_me} HAYES. — May 24, at Wheatleigh, Douglas-street, Stanmore, James Hayes, M.L.C., aged 77 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Sudden Death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sydney, Monday.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. James Hayes, M.L.C., died suddenly yesterday. He was in the garden talking to his wife, who went away for a few moments,When she returned she found her husband in a state of collapse on the verandah, and '= before medical aid 
2 CONC arrived Mr. Hayes had died. The deceased appeared to be com paratively well when in the city on the previous day. He was 77 years of age.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1908 'Family Notices', The Sydney Mail and New South Wales Advertiser (NSW : 1871 - 1912), 27 May, p. 1417. , viewed 26 July 2025, http://nla.gov.au/nla.news-article165394768
