1 NOTE {geni:about_me} WALKER-The funeral of Mrs. Maryette C. Walker was held yesterday morning in the Eden Ward chapel. Bishop's counsellor Virgil P. Stallings conducted the service. The musical numbers were as follows: Solo, "Not Half 
2 CONC Has Even Been Told," by Wilmer Ferrin; solo, "I Know That My Redeemer Lives," by Miss Marba Ferrin; duet, "Beautiful Isle of Somewhere," by Mrs. Ollie Graham and Miss Marba Ferrin. The latter two singers also sang a duet, "In the 
2 CONC Sweet By and By." The closing number was a duet by Wilmer and Marba Ferrin, entitled, "Shall We Meet at the River." The speakers at the funeral were Apostle David. O. McKay, A. B. Thompson, Mrs. Mary A. Jost, Josiah L. Ferrin and 
2 CONC Bishop George A. Fuller. The interment was made in the Huntsville cemetery. The grave was dedicated by George A. Larkin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Published in THE OGDEN STANDARD, January 01, 1918, 2 PM City Edition page 8, Image 8. (Ogden City, Utah) 1913-1920.
