1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The above photo depicts Della Rose Walker Ferrin and her parents and siblings.  It was found on Find A Grave.com.  Depicted in the photo, back row, Charles, Eliza, John, Della, and Effie;  middle row, Lester, John 
2 CONC (father), Maryette (mother), and Levi;  front row, Geneva, Clave and Elva.  The photo was probably taken about 1890.  Following is Della's obituary:
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Della Walker Ferrin, 81, of Lyman, Wyoming, died Sunday in a Provo hospital of natural causes. Mrs. Ferrin was born March 13, 1882, in Eden, Utah, a daughter of John and Mariette Colvin Walker.  She was married to C. LeRoy Fe
2 CONC rrin on June 5, 1900, in the Salt Lake Temple.  He died in 1949.  She had resided in Eden, Lyman and Ogden.  She was active in the LDS Church and Daughters of Utah Pioneers.  Surviving are four sons and one daughter, Floyd L. Ferr
2 CONC in, Leo J. Ferrin, both of Bountiful; Marvin J. Ferrin, Hilo, Hawaii; Sheridan J. Ferrin, San Bernardino, California; Mrs. Phillip (Lydia) Bott, Ogden; 21 grandchildren, 42 great-grandchildren, three brothers and one sister, Charl
2 CONC es H. and L. O. Walker, Lyman; Clave Walker, Henderson, Nev.; Mrs. Geneva Moyes, Twin Falls, Idaho.  Funeral services will be held Wednesday at 11 a.m. in the Larkin Chapel of the Dawn in Ogden. Friends may call at the mortuary Tu
2 CONC esday from 7 to 9 p.m. and Wednesday prior to services. Burial in Eden Cemetery. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Ogden Standard Examiner, Monday Evening, August 26, 19633.
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCE:  Find A Grave.com
