2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary for Lester Vernal Walker:  Funeral services for Lester Walker, 57, of Green River, who died Monday following an automobile accident Saturday at Eden, Utah, were held Thursday at 2 p.m. and the L.D.S. church in Green River
2 CONC . Bishop Lee Nebeker conducted the services and burial was held in Riverview cemetery.  Walker was born February 22, 1892, in Eden and was a son of John and Maryette Colvin Walker.  He married Jessie Kidman of Ft. Bridger, in 1921
2 CONC .  He was employed as a boilermaker in the Union Pacific railroad shops at Green River.  He belonged to the Boilermakers union and to the Association of Railway Employees.  Survivors include:  his wife, Mrs. Lester Walker of Green
2 CONC  River;  three sons, Robert Walker, Laramie; Cecil Walker, Casper; and Arlo Walker, Green River, and one sister, Mrs. James Petre, Los Angeles, California.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:  
2 CONT
2 CONT Rock Springs Miner, July 31, 1949
2 CONT
