1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rock Springs Daily Rocket-Miner, Sep 22, 1984
2 CONT LELAN DAVID BLUEMEL
2 CONT
2 CONT SALT LAKE CITY?Services for Lelan David Bluemel, 77, of Lyman were conducted Saturday, Sept. 15 at the Lyman LDS Stake Center.
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial was in the Lyman City Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bluemel died Monday, Sept. 13 in a Salt Lake City hospital.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born May 21, 1907 in Lyman to Henry John and Melissa Jane Stewart Bluemel.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Ava Maryett Walker Oct. 20, 1928 in Green River. She died Sept. 23, 1935.
2 CONT
2 CONT He later married Thora Rebecca Walker Sept. 14, 1936 in the Salt Lake L.D.S. Temple.
2 CONT
2 CONT He worked as a rancher for most of his life, was a member of the L.D.S. Church and was a high priest in the Lyman 1st Ward.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by his wife of Lyman; three sons, Robert L. Bluemel, Rodney C. Bluemel, and Reynold D. Bluemel, all of Lyman; two daughters, Mrs. Alden (Marjorie) Maxfield of Vernal, Utah, and Mrs. David (Ethel) Coates of Sparks, N
2 CONC ev., 30 grandchildren, 36 great-grandchildren, one brother, Rulon Bluemel of Kearns, Utah, four sisters, Mrs. Delmar (Chloe) Gross of Lyman, Liddie Eyre of Evanston, Bertha Hoopes of Lyman and Mrs. Robert (Berlla) Loux of Twin Fal
2 CONC ls, Idaho.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was preceded in death by a daughter, Maryett Bluemel.
2 CONT -------------------------
2 CONT Thanks to Angela Cable for the obit
