1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ethel Jane Bluemell Coates
2 CONT
2 CONT Sparks - Ethel Jane Bluemel Coates, 89, of Sparks died July 16, 2021. Ethel was born in Lyman, Wyoming on March 29, 1932 to Leland David Bluemel and Ava Maryett Walker. Ethel's mother died when she was three, leaving Leland and th
2 CONC ree small children. Ava's sister, Thora, helped care for the children and eventually married Leland and raised Ava's children and her own. Ethel grew up milking cows and helping in the hay field. In the high school band, she playe
2 CONC d the clarinet.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ethel met David Allison Coates in Cheyenne, WY and they were married June 17, 1951 in Lyman. Their marriage was later solemnized in the Logan, Utah Temple. Ethel served in many ward and stake organizations in the LDS church. She s
2 CONC erved as Relief Society President, and as Florence Drake PTA president at the same time. Following David's retirement from the railroad, David and Ethel served a mission in the Fort Worth, Texas area, and as temple workers in the 
2 CONC Reno Temple. Her favorite place to serve was in her home as a homemaker.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is preceded in death by two brothers: Reynold and Robert, a sister, Marjorie; husband, David A. Coates; a son, Neal David Coates, and a great-grandson, Jaden Pfeil. Surviving are: a brother, Rodney Bluemel (Nola) of Lyman, WY;
2 CONC  a son, Mark A. Coates (Colleen) of Sparks; daughters, Meg Gray of Spring, TX; Linda James (Don) of Riverton, UT; Adel Pfeil (Mike) of Fishers, IN; and Dian Hoff (Randy) of Parker, CO; 17 grandchildren and 33 great grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT A funeral service is scheduled for 11:00 AM, Wednesday, August 4, 2021 at the LDS church in Lyman, WY. Burial will follow at Lyman Cemetery, under the direction of Walton's Funerals and Cremations - Sparks and Crandall Funeral Hom
2 CONC e, Evanston, WY.
