1 NOTE {geni:about_me} from The Bridger Valley Pioneer, Friday, February 7, 1997
2 CONT
2 CONT ROBERT L. BLUEMEL
2 CONT MAY 13, 1934 -- FEB. 4, 1997
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert L. Bluemel, 62, died on Feb. 4, 1997 at Evanston Regional Hospital. Funeral services will be held on Saturday, Feb. 8, at 11 a.m. at the Lyman L.D.S. Stake Center. Friends may call at the church from 9:30 to 10:45 a.m. on S
2 CONC aturday. Interment will follow in the Lyman Cemetery.
2 CONT Robert was born May 13, 1934, in Lyman to Leland David and Ava Margaret (Walker) Bluemel. On June 9, 1955, he married Peggy Ann Slagowski in the Salt Lake L.D.S. Temple.
2 CONT An active member of the L.D.S. Church, Robert served in the Elder's Quorum and as Sunday School President.
2 CONT Robert was a lifelong resident of Lyman. He loved ranching, being with his family, horseback riding and spending time in the mountains. Most of all he loved his grandchildren. He was known for his generosity and for being a pranks
2 CONC ter. Robert will be missed by many.
2 CONT He is survived by his wife, Peggy Ann Bluemel, of Lyman; sons Alan Robert (Laura) Bluemel of West Valley, Utah, Barry Lynn (Brenda) Bluemel of Lyman, Evan Dee (Emma) Bluemel of Millburne, Stacey Glen (Carla) Bluemel of Mountain Vi
2 CONC ew and Stan David (Wilma) Bluemel of Lyman; daughters Edyth Ava (Steven) Bluemel Matthews of Lyman and Peggy Janeel (Bobby) Parker of Sacramento, Calif; his mother, Thora Walker Bluemel of Lyman; brothers, Rodney Bluemel of Lyman 
2 CONC and Reynold Bluemel of Sandy, Utah; and sisters Marjorie Lee Maxfield of Vernal, Utah, and Ethel Jane Coates of Sparks, Nevada.
