1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lawrance Henry Lowell "Jug", 80, passed away on Thursday, June 3, 2021 at his home in Green River, Wyoming. He was born August 11, 1940 in Rock Springs, Wyoming, the son of Lourin Lawrance Lowell and Belva Walker.
2 CONT Lawrance attended schools in Green River and graduated from Lincoln High in 1958.
2 CONT He married Sonia Maldonado in 1963 and had three sons, Lamar, Kevin, Craig. They later divorced.
2 CONT He married Carol Rosine Banzhaf in 1975 and had a daughter, Joanna and a son, Lourin.
2 CONT Lawrance was a Navy veteran who served during the Vietnam era after enlisting in 1958.
2 CONT He worked on the Flaming Gorge Dam, drove Taxi in Salt Lake City before working for Union Pacific Railroad until his retirement.
2 CONT Lawrence was a member of The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints.
2 CONT Jug was known for his active rolls in UPRR Oldtimers, Jr. Oldtimers, toured with the Freedom Bell, National Pony Express Rider Assoc., WY Territorial Gunfighter, Society for Creative Anachronism (SCA), and his William Cody-Buffalo
2 CONC  Bill portrayals.
2 CONT His interests were bowling, playing guitar, playing cards, camping, fishing, working at his business, Jug's Toot and Shoot (gunsmith/toy train shop), taxi driving, and riding in the Flaming Gorge Days & Red Dessert Roundup parades
2 CONC .
2 CONT Survivors include his wife and children & their spouses & families, his 2 brothers & 3 sisters & their spouses & families, aunts Helen Walker & Donna Walker; sister-in-laws Beth Banzhaf & Shirlee Banzhaf; 23 grandchildren; 4 great
2 CONC -grandchildren; 1 great-great-grandchild as well as many cousins, nieces & nephews.
2 CONT He was preceded in death by his parents, brother Vern, nephew Bobby Covington, and numerous in-laws, nephews, nieces, cousins, aunts & uncles.
2 CONT Funeral services will be held at 10:00 am, Friday, June 11, 2021 at The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints, 1000 W 4th N St., Green River, WY. A viewing will be held from 6-8 pm Thursday, June 10, 2021 at the church and o
2 CONC ne hour prior to services on Friday.
2 CONT Interment with military honors will take place at the Riverview Cemetery following the service.
2 CONT Condolences may be left for the family at foxfh.com
