1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rock Springs Daily Rocket-Miner, Sep 20, 1975
2 CONT VERN RAY LOWELL
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services for Vern Ray Lowell, 22, of 502 Schultz, Green River, were conducted Thursday at 1 p.m. at the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints Green River Third Ward Chapel, Bishop David Dawson officiating. Burial was
2 CONC  in Riverview Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Lowell died Sunday, Sept. 13 of injuries he sustained in a one-car accident 1.2. miles west of Green River.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born Dec. 5, 1952 in Rock Springs, he was the son of Lourin L. and Belva Walker Lowell.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was graduated from Lincoln High School in Green River in 1971 and was a member of the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints. He was employed by Adams Trailer Sales and was a member of the Green River Emergency Squad.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include his parents, Green River; three brothers, Lawrence and Ralph, Green River and Rex of Boise, Idaho; three sisters, Ruth Covington and Mrs. Chester (Alice) Capehart, both of Coursicana, Tex. and Mrs. John (Virginia
2 CONC ) Price of Green River.
2 CONT
2 CONT Obit courtesy of Angela Cable
