2 FILE https://www.geni.com/images/documents/doc.png
2 FORM txt
2 TITL Death Certificate
1 NOTE !No record could be found of Martha's birth.  It was necessary to secure in writing from 2 sources old enough at the time of her birth to verify her birth.  This situation was further complicated by the fact that the exact year wa
2 CONC s not known or the correct spelling of her middle name.  Martha was 78 at the time we started working on this verification thus making all sources in their 80s.  Her sister, Eva Blanchard was used as one source.  It was thought th
2 CONC at Martha was 3 years younger than her sister Eva, so the year 1902 was used.  The Historical Department of the LDS church then issued a Certificate of Birth.  That certificate has her middle name spelled Meranda,  whereas it was 
2 CONC thought her middle name was spelled Maranda.  There are now other sources that indicate she was born in 1903.  
2 CONT !In researching this line, it was found that no record exists of the sealing or marriage for Martha's parents.  Previous info indicated that they were sealed & married on the same day they took out their endowments; however, there
2 CONC  is no record of this being so.  All available records were checked.  This problem was taken (by Darleen Wells) to Bro. Val D. Greenwood, Group Manager, Special Services in the church office building.  His staff researched this se
2 CONC aling again and found nothing.  Bro. Greenwood said that the sealing of the husband and wife would have to be done and the children sealed to them.  Reference letter in poss of Darleen Hooton Wells family, dated 9 May 1978.
2 CONT !Maranda often misspelled Miranda. Known as Randy.
2 CONT Blessed: 1 Feb 1903 by Joseph Wall Sr.
2 CONT Baptised by Henry Bluemell
2 CONT Confirmed 2 Sep 1911 by Carl C. Oleand
2 CONT Much later Martha's mother's journal was found and a page of this journal read that Martha was born 1 Nov 1902 in Lyman, Wyoming and was blessed 1 Feb 1903 by Joseph Wall in Lyman, Wyoming, and that she was baptized in 1910 by Bro
2 CONC . Bluemell in Lyman, Wyoming, and that s
2 CONT he married James Raymond Hooton by Bishop James Brown at Evanston, Wyoming, on 1 Nov 1919.
2 CONT This journal also confirms that Martha's middle name is spelled MARANDA.
1 SOUR
2 DATA
3 DATE 20 APR 2020
3 TEXT Date of Birth
