2 TITL Eden, Utah LDS Ward Records
1 NOTE !No record can be found for the death of this child. All state and county records have been checked, as well as cemeteries in Eden and all surrounding areas. It is believed by living members of the family in 1981 (Orlen, David, So
2 CONC phia, Martha) that she died as a child, and information given to Orlen by his mother indicates that she died 1 Aug 1887. However, on film #025921, Eden, Utah Ward record, it indicates that she was baptized 4 Sep 1898. On 11 Jun 19
2 CONC 81 Darleen Wells visited with Bro. Larry Bangerter, Special Services, and he said that because there was no proof of death for this child, work could not be done for her until a 110 years after her birth. Reference; `From You To Y
2 CONC our Ancesters' 1980 edition, page 87. She needs to have her endowments and be sealed to her parents. 
2 CONT !Further research needs to be done. It is confusing because neither Martha or Sophia remember another girl in the family. If May lived to be baptized at age 11, it would be reasonable that there would have been some conversation a
2 CONC bout May in the family during the following years.
2 CONT !Sealing to Parents completed per Temple Submission Record 325-7823
2 CONT !NOTE -Much later an entry was found in her mother's journal confirming birth date and that she was blessed 8 Aug 1887 by O. F. Colvin. She died in August 1887 according to this same journal--and so the baptism and endowment work 
2 CONC was evidently not needed.
1 SOUR
