1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *DENNE, Thomas (1577-1656), of St Alphege, Canterbury, Kent and the Inner Temple, London; later of Denne Hill, Kingston, Kent
2 CONT *bap. 1 Sept. 1577, 1st s. of '''Robert Denne, yeoman of Denne Hill and Thomasine, da. of Thomas Dane of St. John’s, Thanet, Kent'''. educ. King’s sch. Canterbury 1589; I. Temple 1598, called 1607. m. by Oct. 1611, Dorothy (bur. 2
2 CONC 1 Aug. 1637), da. of John Tanfield of Copfold Hall, Margaretting, Essex, 2s. (1 d.v.p.) 5da. 1 other ch. d.v.p. suc. fa. 1594. bur. 1 Aug. 1656.1
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1604-1629/member/denne-thomas-1577-1656
2 CONT *_______________________
