1 OCCU Captain
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Pilgrim father who came from London England in 1634 and settled at Windsor CT. Founder of the New England branch of the family and was in the Pequot war and for his service received a grant of land in Fairfield CT 
2 CONC 80 acres. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note : This land grant ( 1671 ) was in what would become the town of Reading, Ct
2 CONT
2 CONT This came from History of Richtie Co, by Minnie Kendall Lowther 1910.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sailed from England on the HOPEWELL in 1634 from London.
2 CONT
2 CONT The families of Old Fairfield Vol. 1, N-) p. 455-
2 CONT
2 CONT served in Pequot War in May 1637 came to Hingham, MA in 1634, rem to Windsor CT with 1st settler, went to new haven 1639, moved to Fairfield by 1652, settled in Westchester NY by 1682 died ca 1685
2 CONT
2 CONT The History of Fairfield, Fairfield County, Connecticut, from the Settlement ...
2 CONT
2 CONT By Elizabeth Hubbell Godfrey Schenck (online at http://books.google.com/books?id=TV8EAAAAYAAJ&dq=The%20History%20of%20Fairfield%2C%20Fairfield%20County%2C%20Connecticut%2C%20from%20the%20Settlement%20...%20%20By%20Elizabeth%20Hubb
2 CONC ell%20Godfrey%20Schenck&pg=PA64#v=onepage&q=Richard%20Osborn&f=false )
2 CONT
2 CONT one record states father is thomas, one richard also spouse Elizabeth.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Capt. Richard OSBORN was born circa 1612 in London, ENGLAND. He sailed in the Hopewell for Barbados on 17FEB1634, and immigrated on 1Nov1634 to Boston, Suffolk Co. MA. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was in Hingham MA by 1635, then removed to Windsor with the original settlers. He served in the Pequot War in 1637 for which he was given 80 acres in Fairfield (in 1671) for his service. He was named in Stiles HISTORY of WINDSO
2 CONC R as a participant in the Mystic Fort Fight. He removed to New Haven CT in 1639, and was one of 55 signers of the Fundamental Agreement 4JUN1639. He took the oath of allegience in 1644 . He eventually moved to Westchester NY where
2 CONC  he died 8FEB1684.
