1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In the newspaper death notices for both grandsons Matthew Horace Hayes, died 1904, and George Horace Hayes, died 1912, is recorded "son of Horace Townsend Hayes, Rochelle [possibly Rochelle House, Old Blackrock Roa
2 CONC d, Cork City, Co. Cork or Castletownroche Townland, Co. Cork] and grandson of George Hayes, Castleview, Cork".
2 CONT
2 CONT Of Castleview, Ballinoroher, Co Cork Millers at Castleview Mill in Ballinoroher and also Spital Mill at Timoleague. Also the Kilcudy Mill near Cork. Castleview Mill about 3 1/2 miles east of Clonakilty on the banks of the Argideen
2 CONC  was built by George Hayes of Spittal Cross, Timoleague before 1805. Here 6000 barrels of flour were ground annually and shipped through Cork chiefly to England. The milling business was carried on by George's eldest son James and
2 CONC  also another son Henry emigrated to Australia where he founded a milling dynasty around NSW. The Hayes family continued to operate the mill until 1853 even though the mills had come into the possession of Francis Bennett of Rosca
2 CONC rberry some time prior to that.
2 CONT --------------------
