1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ireland Marriage registration index record for Bennett Hayes marrying Eliza Hayes, January to March quarter 1846, Bandon registration district, Cork, Vol. 2, P. 611.
2 CONT
2 CONT Parish marriage record for Bennett Hayes marrying Eliza White, on 24 September 1846, at Kilbrogan,Cork,Ireland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Griffiths Valuation for 23 Cavendish Quay, Bandon, Cork, occupier Bennett Hayes, lessor Mrs Elizabeth Tresilian, house, offices, yard & small garden.
2 CONT
2 CONT Griffiths Valuation for 4 Weir street, Bandon, Cork, occupier Bennett Hayes, lessor William Hawkes, stores and kilns.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ireland death record for Bennett Hayes, Bandon registration district, Cork, widower, retired mill proprietor, died 2 June 1883, aged 84, of Phlegmonous Erysipelas, 7 weeks. [Erysipelas is usually caused by the Group A Streptococcu
2 CONC s bacterium, the same bacterium that causes strep throat. The infection results in large, raised red patches on the skin. This is sometimes accompanied by other symptoms, including blisters, fevers, and chills.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Ireland Probate record for Bennett Hayes, ;late of Bandon County, Cork, gentleman, deceased who died 2 June 1883 at same place was proved Cork by David Craig of same place, Esquire, and William Spiller, of Clonakilty in said count
2 CONC y, Clerk of Poor Law Union, executors, effects £282 4s 6d.
