1 NAME Richard /Hayes/
2 GIVN Richard
2 _MARNM Hayes
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1799
2 ADDR
3 CITY Clonakilty
3 STAE Cork
3 CTRY Ireland
1 DEAT
2 DATE 19 AUG 1887
2 ADDR
3 CITY Cork
3 CTRY Ireland
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Richard was the son of George Hayes of Catleview, Clonakilty, Co Cork. He was conferred with B.A. from Trinity college Dublin in 1828.  Entered Trinity College Dublin on 5 Jun 1822, son of George Hayes, gent. Co.Co
2 CONC rk. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was ordained Deacon in 1841 at Cork and Priest in 1842 at Killaloe, Co Clare. He was Curate at Kilmacabee, Ross from 1848 - 1852, curate of East Skull (Ballydehob, West Cork) 1852 - 1867. He was Rector and Vicar at Natlash and 
2 CONC Kildorerry from 1867 - 1875, when he became Rector of Farahay. The parishes of Nathlash and Kildorerry were then united to it.  This parish was the Parish of the Bowens of Bowen's court. Elizabeth Bowen, Irish novelist, wrote a bo
2 CONC ok entitled Bowen's Court and quotes in a diary by the young Bowens:  Mr Henry Bowen's funeral: The hearse arrived about noon. Mr Harry Bowen, Mr Metge and Mr Shea accompanied it. Rev Mr Hayes jr, read the burial service. Papa and
2 CONC  I were there... (the Mr Hayes is Richard's son) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard married in 1833, Mary Jenkins daughter of William Jenkins AM, MB TCD and had issue George and Richard Thomas in holy Orders, now Rector of Mahgouney, and four daughters Cathleen Tresilian, Mary Elizabeth, Dora Christine an
2 CONC d Adelaide Anne Wilhelmina. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr Hayes resigned 1883 and died on August 19th 1887 in his 84th year at Geyshell's House. (Brady's clerical Records of Cork, Cloyne and Ross) 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1876 Landowners lists Rev. R. Hayes as owning 25 Acres of land valued at 10 pounds 55 shillings at Kildorrery, called 'Rockmills'. Not sure if this is the father or son who owned the land. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Buried at the Church of Ireland, Clonakilty with his wfe.  MI  In loving memory of Rev Richard Hayes, late rector of Farahy, Died August 19th 1887, also of Mary his wife died April 7th 1873. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ireland Probate record for the Reverend Richard Hayes late of Myshells House Cork, clerk, who died 19 August 1887 at same place, was proved at Cork by Rev. Richard Thomas Hayes of Magourney Rectory, in said county. Rector one of e
2 CONC xecutors. Effects £908 5s 5d
