1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In the newspaper death notices for both Matthew Horace Hayes, died 1904, and George Horace Hayes, died 1912, is recorded "son of Horace Townsend Hayes, Rochelle [possibly Rochelle House, Old Blackrock Road, Cork Ci
2 CONC ty, Co. Cork or Castletownroche Townland, Co. Cork] and grandson of George Hayes, Castleview, Cork". In his book "Of men and horses", Matthew Horace Hayes describes how he had a stepbrother (ie George Horace Hayes) who had gone to
2 CONC  Australia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage record for Horace Hayes marrying Margaret Williamson, Diocese of Cork & Ross, County Cork, Ireland, 1831.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife Margaret died in 1834.
2 CONT
2 CONT Southern Reporter and Cork Commercial Courier 19 August 1834, p. 3.
2 CONT
2 CONT Died. On Friday morning at her father's house, Warren's Place, in the bloom of life after a few hours illness, Margaret, the beloved wife of Horace Hayes, of Kilcully Mills, Esq. In this sudden and unexpected dispensation of provi
2 CONC dence, her afflicted family have to mourn the bereavement of an amiable and affectionate wife, a tender mother, and a dutiful daughter. but they "sorrow not as those who have no hope" her early piety and christian walk, gave evide
2 CONC nce that their loss is her unspeakable gain.
2 CONT
2 CONT Horace remarried in 1836. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Southern Reporter and Cork Commercial Courier 11 February 1836, p. 2.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married. This morning at St Nicholas's Church, by the Rev. J.N. Lombard, Horace Hayes, of Kilcully, Esq., to Eliza, daughter of Mr. Matthew Jamieson, of this City.
2 CONT
2 CONT Southern Reporter and Cork Commercial Courier 3 December 1840, p. 1.
2 CONT
2 CONT Births. On Monday at Kilcully, the Lady of Horace Hayes Esq. of a daughter. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Both Horace and wife Elizabeth went to live with their daughter Elizabeth and son in law The Rev. J.N. Lombard in the village of Cahir in Co. Tipperary.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ireland Death registration index record for Horace Hayes, died aged 70, July-September quarter 1873, Clogheen registration district, County Tipperary, Vol. 14. p. 386.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nenagh Guardian, Saturday, August 23, 1873; Page: 3
2 CONT
2 CONT Deaths. August 21, at the residence of his son-in-law, The Vicarage, Caher, Horace Hayes, Esq., late of Cork, age 70 years. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Argus (Melbourne, Vic., Tuesday 21 October 1873, page 4
2 CONT
2 CONT HAYES. — In August, at the vicarage, Cahir, residence of his son-in-law, Rev. F. Cooper, Horace - tenth son of the late George Hayes, of Castleview, County Cork, Ireland, aged 71 years. (Notice would have been placed by son George
2 CONC  Horace Hayes)
2 CONT
2 CONT Ireland Probate registration record for Horace Hayes, formally of the City of Cork, and late of Cahir, County Tipperary, merchant deceased who died 21 August 1873 at Cahir. Proved at Waterford by the oath of Eliza Hayes of Cahir, 
2 CONC the widow and sole executrix. Effects under £200. 
