1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Newnham-158
2 CONT
2 CONT 1787: At the age of 18, Philadelphia married 31 year old Thomas Allchorne (born in Buxted, bap. 15-Aug-1756) on 11-Oct-1787 in Isfield, though the marriage process appears to have begun in Buxted, indicating that Philadephia might
2 CONC  have been living in Buxted [9] [10] [11].
2 CONT
2 CONT 1788-1797: Philadelphia and Thomas then had three children, all baptised in Buxted: 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Thomas 13-Apr-1788 [12], 
2 CONT # George 5-Jan-1794 [13], and 
2 CONT # John 16-Apr-1797 [14]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas remained in Buxted, married Jane Killick (21-Nov-1820)[15] and eventually died in Buxted on 30-Jun-1866 [16]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT George had a more interesting life. In 1816, at the age of 22, George was in the Sussex Assizes charged with Larceny, but was acquitted [17]. In 1831 he was charged with receiving stolen good and convicted on 10-Dec-1831 [18]. He 
2 CONC was sentenced to transportation for 7 years, and sent to Van Diemens Land, where he spent the rest of his life. He ended up reconnecting with his younger half-brother Jonathan Harris (another convict) - and was a witness to Jonath
2 CONC an's third wedding in Tasmania in 1853. He died on 26-Jan-1867 in Tasmania at the age of 74 [19].
2 CONT
2 CONT John, like his brother Thomas, remained in Buxted eventually died and was buried on 28-Oct-1832 [20].
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 1797: Thomas Allcorn, at the age of 41, died on 1-Oct-1797 in Buxted [21], leaving Philadelphia a widow.
