2 CONT '''Lithgow Mercury (NSW : 1898 - 1954)   Fri 14 Jul 1916  Page 6  WEDDING AT KATOOMBA.
2 CONT WEDDING AT KATOOMBA:'''
2 CONT A quiet wedding was celebrated in the Catholic Church, Katoomba, by Rev. Father Bridge; recently, when Albert Frederick, fifth' son of Mrs. R Kirk, Duckmaloi, was married to Mary, eldest daughter of Mr. and Mrs. E.Dwyer, of Duckma
2 CONC loi. After the ceremony the happy couple left by the mail train for Sydney, where the honeymoon was spent. Mr.and Mrs. Kirk will reside in Lithgow.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT NSW BDM Death KIRK ALBERT FREDERICK H 24553/1936 ROBERT ATHELIA LITHGOW
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lithgow Mercury (NSW : 1898 - 1954)  Mon 14 Dec 1936  Page 2  LITHGOW DEATHS'''
2 CONT MR. A. F. KIRK
2 CONT Mr. Albert Frederick Hartley Kirk,who died iin Lithgow hospital yesterday afternoon, was a well-known figure in the district, where he had lived practically all his life. In his young days ne was a noted horseman, and won many pri
2 CONC zes at shows and other meetings with his horses. He was an expert horse-breaker.
2 CONT Mr. Kirk was born at Hartley 67 years ago. He was one of the early employees at the State mine, and worked there as a surface hand for 11 years. Five years ago, however, he 'was obliged to retire owing to illhealth. His condition 
2 CONC had been indifferent since then, and he entered the hospital five weeks ago.
2 CONT To the widow, Mrs. Mary Kirk, of 20 Lett-street, and her son, Mr. Harold Kirk, the sympathy of the community will be extended.
2 CONT The funeral lias been arranged for this afternoon, interment to take place in the Church of England portion of Bowenfels cemetery
2 CONT Messrs.- Matthews and Lemon have, the arrangements in hand.
2 CONT
