2 CONT '''Lithgow Mercury (NSW : 1898 - 1954)  Mon 14 Oct 1912  Page 1  DUCKMALOI.'''
2 CONT DEATH OF AN EX-RESIDENT.
2 CONT (From our own Correspondent.)
2 CONT Profound regret is expressed in this locality at the sad news of the sudden death of an ex-Duckmaloi resident, namely, Mr.Charles Kirk. The deceased came, at the age of about eight years, with his parentsto . reside at Duckmaloi, 
2 CONC and as an ex-pupil of that school he remained until a few years ago a resident of Duckmaloi, when ne married and went to live at Katoomba, at which place he died. The end was sudden and unexpected. Word was received by his aged mo
2 CONC ther on Saturday that Charles was ill, and on Monday morning, at an early hour, Mr.J.Kirby, of Megalong, arrived with tidings of a most serious nature. Mrs. Kirk, accompanied by her son Leslie, at once drove to Katoomba, but blood
2 CONC  poisoning had done its work. The deceased has left a widow and two little children. 'Sincere sympathy is expressed for the bereaved ones, and particularly for the mother, who has long passed the allotted span of life. Old Duckmal
2 CONC oi pupils unite in tendering their sincere sympathy to the brothers and sisters and mother of their old school mate.
2 CONT KATOOMBA, Wednesday,
2 CONT I regret to report the death of Mr. Chas.(Charlie) Kirk, on Monday last, from blood poisoning. Mr. Kirk, during the course of his duty with Messrs. Gearon and Summer greene,' butcher, slightly scratched cne of
2 CONT his arms, and despite immediate attention, blood poisoning supervened, with fatal results.
2 CONT
