1 NOTE !BIRTH DATE AND PLACE OF RESIDENCE AND FATHER'S NAME FROM MARRIAGE
2 CONT CERTIFICATE, A COPY IN POSSESSION OF ANNE CLARK, SUBMITTER.
2 CONT FATHER: THOMAS RANGER, CARPENTER.  DEATH CERTIFICATE STATES THAT HERBERT'S
2 CONT MIDDLE NAME IS EDWARD, BUT I TEND TO BELIEVE THAT THE MARRIAGE CERTIFICATE IS
2 CONT MORE ACCURATE.
1 NOTE Birth date and place of residence and father's name from marriage certificate, a copy in possession of Anne Clark.  Father:  Thomas Ranger, carpenter.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1881 British Census states that Herbert was 20 and his occupation was "groom."  Address: 8 Tovil Hill, East Farleigh, Kent, England.  Herbert was living with his widowed mother and sister, Alice Wood, and adopted brother, Frank Bo
2 CONC ozer.  The latter were sorters in the paper mill.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1891 Herbert is not in the Census and his wife is listed as a widow.
2 CONT "Herbert Edward" was on Ellen Jane Tree Ranger's death certificate, as her husband, but Herbert Edward is her son.   On Herbert Henry Ranger's death certificate it is Herbert Henry.  Died at age 29.  Occupation:  night watchman.  
2 CONC His mother, Harriet Tomsett was the informant.  She was present at his death and she lived on Wyatt Street, Maidstone.  According to the 1881 Census, Harriett, Henry's mother was a widow, so this all fits.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death Certificate in Anne Clark's possession.  Herbert Henry died at Farleigh Hill, East Farleigh, Maidstone, Kent, England.
