1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/collection-1/myheritage-family-trees?itemId=124854591-13-5585&action=showRecord&indId=externalindividual-b3f969d5627c2d94bd7cd919c2128f0b&mrid=86bf5443b51d01d060aa9
2 CONC 86fcf6ded9a MyHeritage Family Trees] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 4 2016, 22:43:00 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary:  Logan, Utah - Cecil L. Walker, 83, passed away peacefully and surrounded by his loving family on August 27, 2003, in Logan, Utah.  Born Cecil Lester Walker on December 3, 1919, in Lyman, Wyoming, to Lester Vernal Walker
2 CONC  and Jessie Kidman Walker.  Cecil was a geologist by profession.  He was also an accomplished artist, master builder, and avid outdoorsman.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cecil was a faithful, active member of The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter Day Saints and loved his Heavenly Father. Cecil always remained close to his family and had a tremendous influence on those that knew him.  His fishing tr
2 CONC ips (and other family outings) will always be remembered with a smile.  He always had a special place in his heart for his grandchildren and great grandchildren and they will forever be blessed by his memory and love.
2 CONT
2 CONT He will be greatly missed by his wife of 60 years Geneva, one son, David (Carolyn) Walker, Riverton, Utah, daughters, Sherry (Steve) Broadbent, Lehi, Utah, Barbara (Rod) Blackford, Highlands Ranch, Colorado, and Cindy (Ken) White,
2 CONC  North Logan, Utajh.  He is also survived by two brothers, Robert (Maizie) Walker, Cheyenne, WYyoming, Orlo (Zolene) Walker, Centerville, Utah, and 25 grandchildren, and 19 great grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services for Cecil Walker will be Saturday, August 30, 2003 at the Logan 10th Ward Chapel, 792 North 500 East at 10:30am. Friends may call from 9:30am to 10:15am on Saturday prior to services. Interment will be in the Loga
2 CONC n Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family would like to extend a special thanks to Laura (granddaughter) for the loving care that she extended to her favorite "patient". The family would also like to thank the IHC hospice team (Bill and Margi) and Dr. Nash (and
2 CONC  staff) for their wonderful support and care.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral arrangements are under the direction Allen- Cranney Mortuary in North Logan. We will miss you Pa! 
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCE:  Find A Grave.com
