1 NOTE /!When Jack served in the Army in World War II, it was discovered that there was a misspelling of the surname on his birth certificate; Hooten instead of Hooton. Army officials required that he use "Hooten" while in the service. U
2 CONC pon returning home, he continued to use this spelling of his surname.
2 CONT Blessed January 11, 1927 by Darius Syme, in Lyman, WY
2 CONT Baptized June 15, 1935 by Joseph Glen Slugowski, Lyman, WY
2 CONT Confirmed June 15, 1935 by Henry C. Voss, Lyman, WY
2 CONT Ordained Deacon March 27, 1938 by Darius M Syme, Lyman, Wy
2 CONT Ordained Teacher March 14, 1943 by Clem G. Eyre, Lyman, WY
2 CONT Ordained Priest March 12, 1944 Lyman, WY by Clem G. Eyre
2 CONT Graduated from Primary March 27, 1938
2 CONT Became a Boy Scout 1938
2 CONT Graduated from Junior Seminary May 12, 1940, Lyman WY
2 CONT Graduated from Lyman Grade School May 17, 1943
2 CONT Graduated Senior Seminary May 9, 1943
2 CONT Graduated from Lyman WY HIGH School May 19, 1944
2 CONT Entered US Army
2 CONT Overseas - Japanese front
2 CONT Mustered Out
1 SOUR
