1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT <p>James Albert Doust being the oldest child, became the head of the family at the age of 13, when his father drowned at sea.   Learned the trade of Auto-mechanic and began to repair cars in the family's back yard. This led to the
2 CONC  formation of the Rye Harbour Garage, which is still in operation today. When James Doust died the garage changed hands and became the property of Joy( nee Doust) and Laurie Band. It remained in their control until Laurie's death 
2 CONC in 1987. It was then sold to Lofty, who as of 2003 was still operating the garage.</p><p><p></p></p><p><p>James fought in World War 1 and was captured by the Germans in Belgium. He escaped and was recaptured again shortly afterwar
2 CONC ds. He escaped a second time and was hidden, in a barn,  from the Germans by a women named Marie. After the war he married Florence Masters, and out of respect for " Marie", he named his first daughter Joan Marie Doust.</p><p><p><
2 CONC /p></p><p><p>The following announcement was taken from the Rye Express and was dated 11 January 1974 and was found on page 2...</p><p><p></p></p><p><p>Doust-- On January 3 at Rye Memorial Hospital, James Albert, aged 74 years, of 
2 CONC Oyster Creek, Rye Harbour. Funeral took place at the Church of the Holy Spirit, Rye Harbour, on Wednesday, January 9.</p><p><p></p></p><p><p>And on page 22 the obituary.....</p></p><p><p></p></p><p><p>Mr. J A Doust</p></p><p><p>Th
2 CONC e funeral service for James  Albert Doust, of Oyster Creek, Rye Harbour, took place at the Church of the Holy Spirit, Rye Harbour, on Wednesday. The service was conducted by the vicar of Rye Harbour, the Rev. John E R Williams.</p
2 CONC ><p>Mr Doust died at the Rye, Winchelsea and District Memorial Hospital on Thursday of last week He was 74.
2 CONT === GEDCOM Source ===
