1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John was born 10/06/1871 in Edinburgh, Scotland, the first born of david and jessie. John travlled as a 3 years old on the Geraldine Paget which left Gravesend London 18/09/1874 arrived in Canterbury 27/12/1874. Jo
2 CONC hn Swann brought good woodworking skills into the district - but cricket was his passion. (local legend has it he orginally came to Lowburn because his mother would not allow him to play rugby, and that when he left home her hair 
2 CONC went white)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr John Swann, who died recently at the age of 78, was one of the most respected and popular residents in t)he Cromwell district. Mr Swann, who was born in Edinburgh, arrived at Dunedin with his parents in 1874, and in his early ’
2 CONC teens went to the Cromwell district, where he engaged in goldmining. About 50 years ago Mr Swannto  bought a Crown secion at Lowburn, and developed it into a farm and orchard, where he lived until his retirement a few years ago. D
2 CONC uring a lifetime spent in the district, Mr Swann took a very active part in all matters affecting its welfare. and up to the time of his death he was an active member of the Vincent Hospital Board, Federated Farmers. and a foundat
2 CONC ion member of tht Upper Clutha Fruitgrowers’ Association. He also served on the Lowburn School Committee.
2 CONT
2 CONT A Rugby and cricket enthusiast, he was a member of both Cromwell and Lowburn football and cricket teams for many years, and represented Vincent in both sports. He also served as a member of the Vincent Rugby Subunion;one of the be
2 CONC st-known referees in Central Otago, and a member of the Cromwell Jockey Club. He is survived by his widow and a family of three sons and seven daughters.
