1 NAME Gerard Stanley /Sanders/
2 GIVN Gerard Stanley
2 _MARNM Sanders
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 30 NOV 1871
2 ADDR
3 CITY Southampton
3 STAE England
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 1939
1 OCCU Barrister at Law
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Gerard,
2 CONT
2 CONT Re : Gerard Stanley Sanders (my grandfather).
2 CONT B.1872, Southhampton, Hampshire, son of Henry Ingalton Sanders. M. Ethel Marian Duprey  1904.  Children Joan Marian Sanders (B.1907 Esher Surrey and Anthony Gerard Sanders 1906).  We know that his profession was Barrister at Law, 
2 CONC Middle Temple, London and that he was admitted to the Temple on 14.02.1902 at which time he gave his address and profession  as Solicitor of  Woodside, Mottingham, Kent. At the time of his marriage he gave his address as Villiers 
2 CONC Street, London. At the time of the 1901 aged 29 he was still living at his parents address 42 Archers Road, Shirley Southampton.
2 CONT
2 CONT As said over the weekend I am curious to know when he died, what he died of and where he died. He was the son of a wealthy father and family gossip has that booze  was the problem. I know that he left Gran and  my Mother.penniless
2 CONC  and in straightened circumstances. There is a suspicion that at the time of his death they were living in Surrey (Wonersh) and the place of my Mother's birth Esher, Surrrey is a curious coincidence in the light of subsequent deve
2 CONC lopments.. 
2 CONT
2 CONT If there is anything which you can add to this tangled story will be interesting. I have tried both BMD and the 1901 Census but with only partial success,. Perhaps you have better tools than I ?
2 CONT
2 CONT Thanks very much.
2 CONT
2 CONT Patrick.  
2 CONT
2 CONT PS  Re Conway Web Site. Thanks for this.  I have had a look at this but there is no obvious connection.  But I will look in further detail to see if one of the Conway's escaped and went to Canada. I W ill let you have  a copy of t
2 CONC he Conway Genealogy Report wjich may be helpful.
2 CONT
2 CONT P
2 CONT Gerard,
2 CONT
2 CONT re: Gerard Stanley Sanders.
2 CONT
2 CONT B. 1872 Southampton. Father Henry Ingalton John Sanders b1837, Eton Bucks d.1912 Southampton Mother Eliza (Lizzie)Marian Lewis b.1840 d.1902.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He had a number of brothers and sisters - Barney.  Ingalton b.1866 who became an architect in Southampton; Constance Lizzie b.1871 d. 1968; Charles Phillip who died at sea; Penderell (Jack) Sanders who is supposed to have gone to 
2 CONC California gold prospecting and Mabel Katherine b.1867 d.1977.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thanks
2 CONT Patrick
