2 CONT Martin Lee Gore (born 23 July 1961)[1] is an English songwriter, musician, singer, record producer and DJ. He is one of the founding members of the electronic rock band Depeche Mode[2] and is its primary songwriter.[3] Gore is the
2 CONC  band's guitarist and keyboardist, contributes backing vocals[4] and occasionally provides lead vocals.[5][6] Gore possesses a tenor singing voice which contrasts with Dave Gahan's dramatic baritone. He is also known for his flamb
2 CONC oyant and (sometimes) androgynous stage persona. Gore has also released several solo albums and collaborated with former Depeche Mode member Vince Clarke as part of VCMG.
