1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for CONNECTICUT with the rank of PRIVATE.
2 CONT [http://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A103157  DAR Ancestor #  A103157]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Thomas Shepherd served in 1776 in Capt. Jacob Brockett's 6th Co., 5th Battalion, Wadsworths Bridage. He enlisted 19 May 1777, discharged 19 May 1780, under Capt. Joseph Mansfield, 6th Regt. (Col. Douglas), Connecticut Line. He enl
2 CONC isted as Sergeant, 8 May 1781, discharged 1 Aug 1781, in Capt. William Van Deursen's Co. of State Guards stationed at New Haven. He was listed as an invalid pensioner, Douglas' Regt., wounded by canon shot at Kip's Bay, NY 15 Sept
2 CONC  1776, pension dated 24 Apr 1816. [Connecticut Men in the Revolution, pp. 409, 215,575,667; Connecticut Pension Roll at Yale Library]
2 CONT
2 CONT On 14 Dec 1795, Thomas Shepherd and wife Lydia conveyed to Jesse Goodsell all right to a dwelling house that formerly belonged to Edward Goodsell (Lydia's widow), which Lydia holds the dower. On 16 Feb 1807, Thomas Shepard conveye
2 CONC d to Philemon Augur all right in widow's dower in the estate of father Samuel Shepherd. On 7 Apr 1807 Thomas Shepherd and wife Lydia conveyed to their son Elihu Shepherd our right in the dower which widow Thankful Ludington holds 
2 CONC in the estate of our father Jesse Ludington. On 6 Spet 1813 Thomas Shepherd conveyed to son Elias. On 12 Dec 1834 Thomas Shepherd conveyed to Hervey Chidsey and Lydia his wife, land in East Haven, the said Lydia Chidsey to provide
2 CONC  him with board, lodging and clothing for life. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The last deed was after the death of his third wife, and he died at the home of his daughter, Mrs. Chidsey. 
