1 NAME Darius /Scovil/
2 GIVN Darius
2 SURN Scovil
2 _MARNM Scovill
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 15 MAY 1746
2 ADDR
3 CITY Waterbury
3 STAE Province of Connecticut
3 CTRY British Crown Colony
1 DEAT
2 DATE 3 FEB 1826
2 ADDR
3 CITY Paris
3 STAE New York
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: Full text https://archive.org/details/surveyofscovilso00brai/page/202 "A Survey of the Scovils or Scovills in England and America; Seven Hundred Years of History and Genealogy" by Homer Worthington Bra
2 CONC inard p. 202=203
2 CONT
2 CONT 34. Darius /4 Scovill {William /3, John /2, John /1), born May 15, 1746, at Waterbury; died Feb. 3, 1825, at Paris, N. Y.; married July 4, 1771, at Westbury, now Watertown, Lydia Grannis, born Dec. 16, 1750, at East Haven, Connect
2 CONC icut; died March 15, 1830, at Paris, N. Y.; daughter of Stephen and Hannah (Dawson) Grannis.
2 CONT
2 CONT Darius Scovill resided on Nova Scotia Hill, parish of Westbury, now Watertown. He was a prominent and respected man in the community. In 1758 he was taxed as a churchman and became a communicant of Christ Church, Westbury- Waterto
2 CONC wn. In 1803 he removed to Paris, N. Y., where he purchased a farm from the executors of Gen. George Washington's estate. Here he built a house which was destroyed by fire a few years after his death. He was a prominent man also at
2 CONC  Paris, and one of the founders of St. Peter's Church there.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children horn at Waterbury-Watertown.
2 CONT
2 CONT i. Ascena, born Nov. 4, 1772; died Oct. 23, 1776.
2 CONT
2 CONT ii. Selah, born Oct. 19, 1774; died Oct. 26, 1776.
2 CONT
2 CONT 89. iii. Selah, born Dec. 4, 1776; married Sabra Foote.
2 CONT
2 CONT 90. iv. Asenath, born Jan, 26, 1779; married Henry Allyn.
2 CONT
2 CONT 91. v. Isaac, born Mar. 4, 1781; married Jane Hotchkiss.
2 CONT
2 CONT 92. vi. Seabury, born Jan. 26, 1784; married Abby Safford.
2 CONT
2 CONT 93. vii. Stephen, born June 26, 1786; married Sarah Holmes.
2 CONT
2 CONT 94. viii Edward, born Feb. 16, 1791; married Mary Strong.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
