2 CONT Levi registered with the "State Troops" when he was 16 for the State of Connecticut. He was made a Captain in 1798 by the Governor, Samuel Hutchinson. It is believed he was in 4 Revolutionary War battles. The DAR in Washington, DC
2 CONC  have nothing on Levi, because no one has researched this line.  Levi passed when he was 76. His wife was Lydia, and they had 9 children. Of whom, Orrin and Philo were 8th and 9th, respectively, and they were twins
