1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Arrived in NSW 9 March 1822 per "Isabella". Sentenced to 7 years transportation, he was assigned to Charles Tunstall, a plaster of Lower Minto. Received his Certificate of Freedom 5 May 1828.
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Colonial Secretary Indiex, 1788-1825:
2 CONT
2 CONT LEDWICH, Christopher. Per "Isabella", 1822 1822 Apr 4  On list of prisoners assigned (Fiche 3290; 4/4570D p.71) 1824 Oct 26 Attached to Mr J Blaxland's clearing party; sent to Barracks for attempting to rob a cart. On return of pr
2 CONC oceedings of the Bench of Magistrates, Parramatta (Reel 6023; 4/6671 p.57) 1824 Nov 13 On list of convicts transported to Port Macquarie per "Sally" (Reel 6019; 4/3864 pp.494-5)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Christopher Ledwidge (Ledwich) and his brother James were born and grew up in Dublin, Ireland. Both convicted at County Dublin, James on 3 May 1821 and Christopher 4 May 1821. Christopher was transported to Australia from Cork on 
2 CONC "Isabella"
