1 NOTE !No record existed of the sealing or marriage for this couple. Previous information indicated that they were sealed and married on the same day they took out their endowments; however, there is no record of this being so. All avai
2 CONC lable records have been checked. This problem was taken by Darleen Wells to Bro. Val D. Greenwood, Group Manager, Special Services, in the Church Office Building, and after having his staff research this sealing again, and finding
2 CONC  nothing, he said that the sealing of James Fackrell and Julia Ann Edge would would have to be done again, and their children would have to be sealed to them. This was done in 1982. Reference letter in possession of Darleen Wells 
2 CONC family, dated 9 May 1978.
2 CONT !Bro. Greenwood offered two possible scenarios for their being no record of their sealing and marriage when they took out their endowments. One is that records at the Endowment House sometimes were not maintained properly, and so 
2 CONC the work could have been done, but not recorded. The second is they may have thought the endowment ceremony included all of the ordinances they needed.
2 CONT !James and Julia Fackrell moved from Eden, Weber Utah to Lyman, Uinta, Wyoming on 1 Mar 1902 per entry in Julia Ann's journal.
