0 @N6000000001793317158@ NOTE Child 12 Mary Ann Lucas Born on 23rd December, 1805
1 CONT By: Betty Taber Mary 
1 CONT Ann Lucas was born on 23rd December, 1805 in Sydney. She was the twelfth of thirteen children born to Nathaniel and Olivia Lucas. As with her sister Sarah, she was called Mary after one of the twins who had been killed by a fallin
1 CONC g tree on Norfolk Island. 
1 CONT Nathaniel and Olivia and their nine children, who were still living, were evacuated from Norfolk Island arriving in Sydney on 11th March, 1805. Only the last two of their family were born in Sydney. Mary Ann was baptized at St. Ph
1 CONC ilip's Church, Sydney on 25th December, 1813. She lived in Sydney, with her parents, until the family moved to Liverpool. 
1 CONT Olivia took all the younger children to Van Diemen's Land on the "Sinbad" in 1817, including Mary Ann, and settled at Launceston.
1 CONT Mary Ann married Samuel Cox, another Norfolk Islander, on 24th July, 1822 at Longford. They had twelve children all born Norfolk Plains. The five eldest children were baptized at St. John's, Launceston and the seven youngest were 
1 CONC baptized at Christ Church, Longford after that church was built. Mary Ann and Samuel lived in the vicinity of Norfolk Plains all their lives.
1 CONT Mary died on the 24th July, 1853 at Longford and was buried at Christ Church, Longford. She only outlived her husband, Samuel by five months. He died February, 1853 
1 CONT Children of Mary Ann and Samuel Cox
1 CONT A. John Cox	H. Charles Cox	
1 CONT B. George Cox 	I. Philip Cox	
1 CONT C. Samuel Cox	J. Nathaniel Cox	
1 CONT D. Mary Ann Cox	K. Francis Cox	
1 CONT E. William Cox	L. Alfred James Cox	
1 CONT F. Samuel Cox 	M. Olivia Ambrosine Cox	
1 CONT G. Sarah Cox		
